{"name":"Pomegranate Persian Halloumi","permalink":"pomegranate-persian-halloumi","edit":"https://github.com/The-Silverwood-Institute/Recibase/tree/master/src/main/scala/se/reciba/api/recibase/recipes/PomegranatePersianHalloumi.scala","source":"Gousto","description":"Halloumi coated in ras el hanout, pan-fried until golden and served with pomegranate couscous and caramelised onions.","tagline":null,"notes":[],"dated_notes":[],"tags":["Stephani-ish","Vegetarian","Scales","Hot Weather","Low Effort","Quick"],"inherited_tags":["Stephani","Vegetarian-ish","Pescatarian"],"image":null,"ingredients_blocks":[{"name":null,"ingredients":[{"name":"Halloumi","quantity":"200g","prep":"cut into thick slices","notes":null},{"name":"Couscous","quantity":"125g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Boiled water","quantity":"170ml","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Red onion","quantity":"2","prep":"finely sliced","notes":null},{"name":"Sultanas","quantity":"30g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Pomegranate molasses","quantity":"15g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Pomegranate seeds","quantity":"10g","prep":null,"notes":"optional"},{"name":"Ras el hanout","quantity":"1 tbsp","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Mint","quantity":"10g","prep":"leaves stripped and roughly chopped","notes":null},{"name":"Natural yoghurt","quantity":"80g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Olive oil","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Salt","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Pepper","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null}]}],"method":["Boil a kettle.","Add the couscous and sultanas to a bowl, pour over the boiled water, cover and set aside.","Combine half the ras el hanout in a bowl with a generous grind of black pepper.","Add the sliced halloumi and mix to coat evenly.","Heat a large, wide-based pan (preferably non-stick) with 1 tbsp olive oil over a medium-high heat.","Once hot, add the sliced red onion and cook for 6-7 min or until soft and lightly caramelised.","Fluff the couscous with a fork.","Add the pomegranate molasses, caramelised onions (reserve the pan!), 1 tbsp olive oil and the remaining ras el hanout and mix well.","Combine the chopped mint in a small bowl with the natural yoghurt.","Return the reserved pan to a medium-high heat.","Once hot, add the spiced halloumi and cook for 1-2 min on each side or until golden.","Serve the halloumi over the pomegranate couscous with a garnish of pomegranate seeds."]}